{"query":"Treasury or DWP official guidance October 2020 Job Support Scheme tier 3 unable to work Universal Credit 80% wages","results":[{"date":"Oct 26, 2020","position":1,"site_name":"www.r3.org.uk","snippet":"HMRC have published further information on the Job Support Scheme – including how you can check if you’re eligible and when you can make your first claim.","title":"HMRC – Job Support Scheme (October 2020) - r3.org.uk","url":"https://www.r3.org.uk/technical-library/hmrc-job-support-scheme-october-2020/"},{"date":"Oct 21, 2020","position":2,"site_name":"www.bbc.co.uk","snippet":"The claim: Employees unable to work in tier 3 areas will get a combination of Job Support Scheme and Universal Credit, which will mean they get 80% of their wages. Verdict: While that will be the ...","title":"Covid: Do all tier 3 area workers get 80% of their wages? - BBC","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/54633147"},{"date":"Oct 30, 2020","position":3,"site_name":"payadvice.uk","snippet":"HMRC have published more details and guidance to assist employers in operating and claiming support through the new Job Support Scheme which commences from Sunday 1st November 2020.","title":"Job Support Scheme – Guidance Published (30th October 2020)","url":"https://payadvice.uk/2020/10/30/job-support-scheme-guidance-published-30th-october-2020/"},{"position":4,"site_name":"bhp.co.uk","snippet":"Similar to the Job Support Scheme, where employees receive two-thirds of their wages for time not worked, the grant per eligible employee available from the UK Government is two-thirds of their normal pay up to a limit of £2100 per month. Further detail on how normal pay is calculated will be set out in further guidance by the end of October. Your employer can claim under the rules announced ...","title":"22 October 2020 Job Support Scheme Expansion For Closed ...","url":"https://bhp.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Job-support-scheme-tier-3-22.10.20.pdf"},{"date":"Oct 30, 2020","position":5,"site_name":"www.lexology.com","snippet":"The government is providing support to help businesses retain employees through the Job Support Scheme (JSS). Announced initially on 24 September 2020, the government later announced that the ...","title":"Job Support Scheme - 22nd October 2020 - Lexology","url":"https://www.lexology.com/library/detail.aspx?g=e787acc0-779d-4d1f-9560-9d4237ffcced"},{"position":6,"site_name":"worknest.com","snippet":"Job Support Scheme FAQ On 24 September 2020, the government announced further measures to assist employers and employees in the form of a Job Support Scheme (JSS). This will replace the Coronavirus Job Retention Scheme, which is due to come to an end on 31 October 2020.","title":"Job Support Scheme FAQ","url":"https://worknest.com/covid-19/partnerships/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Job-Support-Scheme-FAQ.pdf"},{"date":"Oct 12, 2020","position":7,"site_name":"www.aatcomment.org.uk","snippet":"HMRC has published an extensive set of updates following the launch of the Job Support Scheme, extensions to other Covid-19 support schemes, and preparations for leaving the EU single market. Job Support Scheme (JSS) The Government recently announced the Job Support Scheme (JSS) to protect jobs where businesses remain open but are facing lower demand over the winter months due to COVID-19 ...","title":"HMRC updates and guidance - October 2020 - AAT Comment","url":"https://www.aatcomment.org.uk/trends/coronavirus/hmrc-updates/hmrc-updates-20-october/"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}